  "body": "## What changed\nThe test helpers `pump_until_idle` and `pump_until_confirm` in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/ai_chat/mod.rs` called `Harness::run()` inside a wait loop. They now call `Harness::step()`. `submit_prompt` uses `run_steps(2)`.\n\n## Cause\nPost-merge run 43813475222 failed with `Harness::run exceeded max_steps (4)` at `mod.rs:84` (`pump_until_idle`). The repaint cause was `egui scroll_area.rs:1524`, a scroll animation. On a slow runner the animation outlasts four steps. PR #2102 and PR #2120 do not touch this path: it is a flaky test helper, not a code regression. The Allow/Deny confirmation gate and the test assertions are unchanged.\n\n## Tested\n- `cargo xtask gate test post_confirmation_allow_and_deny --crate camcraft-ui`: ok (on origin/main before the fix, so the failure is timing dependent)\n- `cargo xtask gate test ai_chat --crate camcraft-ui`: ok, all ai_chat tests\n- `cargo clippy -j 6 -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: ok\n\n## Not exercised\nThe failure does not reproduce on a fast machine. The fix is checked by the log reading, not by a forced slow run.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #2137\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
